We need to analyze the problem.

The test scenario:

- There are three tabs: Account (id="tab-account"), Notifications (id="tab-notifications") which is disabled, Billing (id="tab-billing").

Initially, Account tab is selected (aria-selected=true, active class). Then user presses ArrowRight. Expected outcome: move to the next enabled tab skipping disabled Notifications, i.e., select Billing tab (aria-selected=true, focus moves to #tab-billing).

Observed: After pressing ArrowRight, the state shows that the Notifications tab remains selected (still active, aria-selected=true) and focus didn't move to Billing. Actually looking at "after" snapshot: In the after state, we see:

